:"Electronic dance musician from the UK, also runs the label [l=Astrophonica].\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:434256","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":610845,"name":"Charlie Fieber"},{"id":2792257,"name":"Dawn Day Night"},{"id":7028030,"name":"Hot Source (3)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["DJ Fracture"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/434256-Fracture-2","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.twitter.com/charliefracture","http://www.facebook.com/fracture","http://www.astrophonica.co.uk","http://www.soundcloud.com/fracture-official","http://www.mixcloud.com/fracture"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/43844/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"43844","image":"https://i.discogs.com/VTwm1meWBBIwb0Cpn0uJdo9dTCeaXuIrSmRwRPt4MlU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:405/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQzODQ0/LTE1MDQ4NjE4NTEt/OTQ5MC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/A1FoUAPXCeY7xI1uPSFwt9g4pTjbU83NUIhJco5dkGs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQzODQ0/LTE1MDQ4NjE4NTEt/OTQ5MC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"La Bouche (IPA : [la buʃ]) was a Eurodance act based in Germany, fronted by American-German singer [a62722]. Their most successful hit \"Be My Lover\" was top 10 across Europe and peaked at #6 on the Billboard Hot 100 in 1996. The group was the brainchild of German producer [a76398]. In 2000, after [a62722] left the group to pursue a solo career, she was replaced by [a40772] with a single called \"All I Want\". This track didn't chart well, though, and the group disbanded. Meanwhile, [a62722] was achieving large sales with \"Wonderful Dream\" and was chosen by Coca Cola to perform the theme song for a Christmas Commercial. While promoting this, [a62722] was killed in a plane crash near Zurich, Switzerland, on November 24th 2001.\r\n\r\nIn April 2002, Farian compiled songs from Thornton's album along with selections from the first and second La Bouche albums into a best of collection entitled The Best of La Bouche (feat. Melanie Thornton).\r\n\r\nIn November 2002, one year following Thornton's death, Farian prepared a tribute single entitled \"In Your Life\", a song which had been previously unreleased. Farian combined her vocals with [a=Kayo Shekoni] from [a=Le Click], who provided additional vocals to complete the mix. The single was released worldwide in 2002 and in the U.S. in 2003. It peaked at number 9 on the Hot Dance Club Play chart.\r\n\r\nIn 2007 a 3-track EP was released on iTunes under the name 'Le Click' titled \"Let's Click: 90's Dance Classics.\" These are 3 tracks from the S.O.S & A Moment Of Love album recording sessions that didn't make the cut.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:43844","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":377639,"name":"Stars For Children"}],"members":[{"active":false,"id":40772,"name":"Natascha Wright"},{"active":false,"id":62722,"name":"Melanie Thornton"},{"active":false,"id":157459,"name":"Dana Rayne"},{"active":false,"id":183185,"name":"Kayo Shekoni"},{"active":true,"id":273071,"name":"Lane McCray"},{"active":true,"id":995817,"name":"Sophie Cairo"}],"namevariations":["Bouche","La Banche","La Boche","La Bouch","La Boushe","La Buche","La Mouche","LaBouche","Labouche"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/43844-La-Bouche","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.officiallabouche.com","","","","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Bouche","http://www.youtube.com/user/LaBoucheVEVO"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4751950/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4751950","image":"https://i.discogs.com/-k3xBDgXqIQWtffPKugoZ1GfN9xI6ki6kA9S-XwtXw0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3NTE5/NTAtMTUzNzY4MTA5/Mi04MDUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/3NpozUutN-ulQHarT5CRfwwbk0zxCP7o9adgt0MYazc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3NTE5/NTAtMTUzNzY4MTA5/Mi04MDUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile"